# ML Model Observability & Drift Monitoring Dashboard (Grafana + Prometheus + Evidently)

## Overview

This project implements a 4-panel **Model Overview** observability dashboard in Grafana backed by Prometheus metrics and an Evidently AI drift scoring pipeline for the xFusionCorp Industries ML platform (`fraud-detector` service). The dashboard surfaces real-time serving throughput, inference latency, prediction accuracy, and per-feature Population Stability Index (PSI) drift side-by-side for rapid on-call triage.

## Monitoring Stack Architecture

* **Flask Metric-Emitter**: Exposes HTTP traffic counters, model inference latency histograms, prediction accuracy gauges, and republished drift scores.
* **Evidently AI Drift Scorer**: Recalculates per-feature PSI drift against a reference dataset every 15 seconds and logs scoring runs to the `fraud-detector drift monitoring` project (`01a1f178-e527-7e9c-a2e8-0568943d0a96`).
* **Prometheus (`http://prometheus:9090`)**: Scrapes application and drift metrics and serves as the pre-provisioned Grafana datasource (`uid: PBFA97CFB590B2093`).
* **Grafana (`http://localhost:3000`)**: Hosts the provisioned `Model Overview` dashboard (`uid: model-overview`) with a 15-second auto-refresh interval.

## Dashboard Panel Configuration

| Panel ID | Title | Visualization Type | PromQL Query | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `1` | **Request Rate** | `timeseries` | `sum by (version, endpoint, method) (rate(flask_http_request_total[1m]))` | Tracks per-endpoint, method, and model-version request throughput (`req/s`) |
| `2` | **p95 Inference Latency** | `stat` | `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(model_inference_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))` | Displays 95th-percentile inference latency in seconds |
| `3` | **Prediction Accuracy** | `gauge` | `prediction_accuracy` | Displays live model prediction accuracy (`0.0`–`1.0` scale) |
| `4` | **Drift by Column (PSI)** | `bargauge` | `data_drift_score` | Compares per-feature PSI drift (`amount`, `hour`, `num_tx_past_day`) |
